    question: 'What is a phantom charge on a hospital bill?',
    answer: 'A phantom charge is a bill for a service that was scheduled or ordered but never actually performed — a cancelled procedure, a medication you did not receive, a consultation that was planned but did not occur, or a supply item that was not used. These are often caught only when you compare the itemized bill line by line to your own memory of what actually happened during your stay. Keep a personal log during any hospital admission.',
